Step 5, pages 11 to 13. Check the target shape to the right of the top arrow. Given the starting assumption on the left, the sum of the squares of the two sides at right angles to the right of the arrow is always equal to the square of the hypotenuse (a squared plus b squared = c squared), which means that we will show why the Pythagorean theorem and the conservation of area conclusion always hold true. Never mix assumptions and conclusions, and now let's build a logical bridge in the proof diagram below!

